# for opensusemaintainer CGI:

run with podman:
podman build -t opensusemaintainer .
podman run -p 8080:80 -v $PWD/db:/var/lib/wwwrun/db:z opensusemaintainer

The image contains no package databases - it only serves them. Build them
first (this downloads a few GB of distro metadata and takes a while):

make fetch
make update

That fills db/ with the .dbm files the mount above exposes to the CGI.
Without them every lookup fails and the page shows a "Database problem"
banner.
